    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d200">

                <pb facs="0464" n="436" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v14p1/pg436"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">396.1 GE/5–2754: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 200<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the United
                        States Delegation at the Geneva Conference</hi><anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d200-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-05-28T14:09:00-04:00">May 28, 1954—2:09
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Tosec 284. Secto 324.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d200-f2"/> It seems clear Chinese
                    Communists are attempting, perhaps with British assistance, to use prisoner
                    issue to bring about direct negotiations between us and Chinese Communists. I
                    have doubts about desirability this course of action, which would probably be
                    given large comment and play in Asia as step toward recognition. Therefore I
                    suggest we should refrain from deputing <pb facs="0465" n="437" xml:id="pg437"/>
                    representative to negotiate with Chinese Communists—at least pending further
                    efforts by Trevelyan.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dulles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d200-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d200-f1-content">
                <p>Drafted by McConaughy and Drumright; revised by Dulles. The last clause in the
                    second sentence appears in Dulles’ handwriting on a preliminary draft attached
                    to the source text; the clause originally read, “which is not likely to produce
                    results better than those obtainable by Trevelyan.”</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d200-f2" n="2" xml:id="d200-f2-content">
                <p><ref target="#d199"><hi rendition="#italic">Supra</hi></ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
